    construction: {"kind":"sponge","feedforward":true,"tag":"Sponge-FP · capacity-side feed-forward","perm":"Dragon-p\n1600 bit · 16 rounds","rateBits":"r = 1024 bit","capBits":"c = 576 bit","capName":"inner","outFrom":"capacity","outLabel":"Truncate inner","outSub":"h ≤ c, no extra permutation","ffLabel":"Save inner before the permutation, XOR back into inner after","note":"X ← P(X) ⊕ (0^r ‖ right_c(X)): only the capacity gets a Davies–Meyer-style feed-forward, the rate does not (the document states that feeding forward the outer part adds no security). Padding pd10*; the last block XORs C = 0^{c−1}‖1 into the capacity, preventing length extension arising from inner output. The digest is read from inner, h ≤ c, and squeezing calls no permutation; the feed-forward also lets the squeeze rate r′ exceed the absorb rate r (XOF-256: r = 1024, r′ = 1280).","ivLabel":"IV = SM3-derived (instance domain string)","finalTag":"Last block C → inner","finalTagNote":"C=0^(c−1)‖1 is injected before saving inner, so C enters both permutation input and capacity feed-forward."},
