    construction: {"kind":"sponge","feedforward":true,"tag":"Feed-forward sponge Sponge-FP · capacity-side feed-forward","perm":"Thunder-p\n1600 bit · 12 rounds","rateBits":"r = 1024 bit","capBits":"inner = 576 bit","capName":"inner","outFrom":"capacity","outLabel":"Truncate inner","outSub":"h < c, zero extra permutations","ffLabel":"Save inner before P, XOR it back into inner after","note":"Only the orange line differs from a standard sponge: S ← right_c(X) saves the absorbed inner part and XORs it back after P, so each call is a non-invertible Davies–Meyer-type map on the inner part only. A standard sponge needs c ≥ 2h for h-bit preimage security (a 1024-bit digest would need a >2048-bit permutation); feed-forward raises preimage security to about min{c, h}, so c = h + 64 suffices and 1600 bits cover up to Thunder-1024. Padding pd10*; the last block XORs C = 0^{c−1}‖1 into the capacity and the digest is read from the inner side, which together block length extension. Mode bounds cite Guo et al. (CRYPTO 2026); the design document only plugs in parameters, without its own proof.","ivLabel":"IV = independent c-bit constant per instance","finalTag":"Last block C → inner","finalTagNote":"Inject last-block C, then save inner, permute and feed forward."},
