    construction: {"kind":"chain","tag":"Counter-bDM · b parallel Davies–Meyer","box":"CF · b parallel branches","boxSub1":"uBlock-1024 · 52 rounds × b calls","boxSub2":"u¹ as plaintext; (b−1)n chaining + (5−b)n message = 1024-bit key","chainBits":"Chaining b × 256 bit (b = 2/3/4)","finalBox":"Last block uses CF′","finalSub1":"Key also XORed with (j + 15) for domain sep.","finalSub2":"Final b blocks are the digest, no truncation","note":"Counter-bDM's key length is fixed at 4n instead of bn and all extra room carries message, raising uHash-512's rate from 1/2 to 3/2; with b = 4 the message is only 256 bits. Padding M‖1‖0* to a multiple of an bits, no length encoding (no MD strengthening). Digest = final b blocks, untruncated.","dmFeedback":true,"dmLabel":"Per-block Davies–Meyer feed-forward: u^j_{i+1} = E_{K_i}(u¹_i ⊕ (j−1)) ⊕ u¹_i; (j−1) is the branch index, unrelated to the message block index","msgLabels":["m1 (key input)","m2 (key input)"],"parallel":{"items":["E_K(u¹ ⊕ 0)","E_K(u¹ ⊕ 1)","⋮","E_K(u¹ ⊕ (b−1))"],"caption":"K = (b−1) chaining blocks ‖ (5−b) message blocks"}},
